From 06b527ea18098c9cd821c728f0c3349f1d8a8159 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 14:04:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03996/11362] [outer-loop] Implement separate-focused-goal-call
 fallback for L2 reinduction (unblocks the real-prompt code-gen failure)

The capture diagnostic (proto_l2_capture/fix_finder) proved the real lp85 L2 reinduction
proposer_FAILS because the model rambles analysis into engine() comments, exhausts max_tokens=2560,
and never writes is_level_complete -- and a budget bump does NOT help. Fix: when the combined
engine+is_level_complete induce fails, fall back to TWO focused calls -- an engine-only call and a
focused is_level_complete-only call (win exemplar front-and-centre) -- so the engine ramble cannot
starve the goal. The combined happy path is unchanged (no regression for the synthetic/online cases).

- LocalGGUFProposer.induce: combined call -> on success write as before; on failure -> _goal_only_prompt
  + engine-only generate + goal-only generate -> _combine_world_model. New helpers _write_world_model
  (with a note so the split is logged), _goal_only_prompt, _combine_world_model.
- generate() gate: drop the redundant `"is_level_complete" in required` so the focused engine-only
  (("engine",)) and goal-only (("is_level_complete",)) calls still get the code-only path; scope is
  carried entirely by codeonly_eligible (induce paths True, refactor False). _L2_CODEONLY_DIRECTIVE
  made generic ("the requested function(s)").

VALIDATED LIVE on the captured real lp85 L2 prompt: the combined call fails, but engine-only (35.4s,
valid) + goal-only (8.6s, valid) -> a parseable combined world model with both defs. Tests: new
test_induce_split_fallback.py (happy-path = 1 call no split; combined-fail -> 3-call focused split;
engine-fail -> blocked, no fabricated model) + engine-only/goal-only gate tests in
test_codeonly_induce_scoping.py. 27 tests pass; ruff + arc-orphan-solver-lint clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
